    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, as the code currently stands. (Note: the active config is `petclinic.security.enable=false` and profile `spring-data-jpa`, per `application.properties` \u2014 this matters at two points below.)\n\n## 1. Security filter chain\n- **Runtime (current config):** `DisableSecurityConfig` \u2014 `anyRequest().permitAll()`, CSRF disabled. The `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the handler is **inert**, because method security is not enabled in this config.\n- **If `petclinic.security.enable=true`:** `BasicAuthenticationConfig` enforces HTTP Basic auth + `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` via the now-active `@PreAuthorize`.\n\n## 2. Request-body binding & validation (on `OwnerFieldsDto`)\nTriggered by `@Valid`/`@Validated`. All failures here become a **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`.\n\n**a. JSR-380 bean constraints on the DTO:**\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words), `@Size(1..30)`\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n- `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n- `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n\n**b. `@InitBinder` custom `Validator`s (these also MUTATE the payload):**\n- `OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice` \u2014 rejects blank required fields; **normalizes `address`** (uppercase, collapse whitespace, expand ST/RD/AVE via `AddressNormalizer`); **rewrites `telephone` to E.164** via `E164Telephone.toE164` (assumes +61, drops leading 0, validates 8\u201315 digits), rejecting telephone if no valid E.164 can be formed.\n- `OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice` \u2014 rejects postcode out of range for the city (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099); unknown cities / null postcode pass.\n\n## 3. `@Before` aspects on the controller method (pre-checks, before handler body)\n- `OwnerDailyLimitAdvice` \u2014 counts owners registered today; throws **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS** at \u2265100.\n- `OwnerCityCapacityAdvice` \u2014 counts owners in the same (normalized) city; throws **409 CONFLICT** at \u226550.\n\n## 4. Handler body (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`)\n- **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `OwnerMapper.toOwner`, whose setters cause side-effects:\n  - `setRegistrationDate` \u2014 defaults null to `LocalDate.now()` and rolls weekends forward to the next business day (`BusinessDay`).\n  - `setEmail` \u2014 lower-cases the email.\n- **Compute and set `customerCode`** = `CustomerCode.of(owner, findAllOwners())` \u2192 `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `NNNN` is a per-city sequence (requires reading all existing owners).\n- Call `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n\n## 5. `@Before` aspect on the service method\n- `OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect` (on `saveOwner`) \u2014 for new owners, builds key `telephone|email|` and throws **409 CONFLICT** if any existing owner matches.\n\n## 6. Persistence\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2192 JPA persist. On flush, **entity-level constraints on `Owner`/`Person`** are enforced: `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, and `telephone` `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern` requiring E.164 format (`^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`) \u2014 which passes only because step 2b rewrote it.\n\n## 7. Audit side-effect\n- `AUDIT` logger writes an audit line (`owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026`).\n\n## 8. Response DTO enrichment (no storage effect)\n- **Map `Owner` \u2192 `OwnerDto`** via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, with four `@AfterMapping` derivations: `householdId`, `identityKey`, `locality`, `contactPreference`.\n- Three `@AfterReturning` aspects enrich the returned DTO: `OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice` (`membershipNumber`), `OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice` (`namesakeCount`, `membershipLevel`), `OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice` (`bulkSignupWarning` when >80 created today).\n\n## 9. Response\n- Return **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Notably absent:** there are no JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`/`@EntityListeners`) and no application events anywhere in this flow."
